{
  "id": "ss.relic.shrink",
  "name": "Runt instar",
  "description": "One grub, small and never finished: white through and through, curled the way a young one lies, head a size larger than the segment behind it with the eye still shut. It is drawn small in the frame on purpose — the plate is left mostly empty around it, and that emptiness is what carries 'less of you' now that the object is a single body rather than a before-and-after pair. Colour is what keeps it apart from the brood in ss.relic.drone, which is this same chain-of-circles recipe in carapace purple inside a yellow cell; this one is bare white on the bare plate, and nothing else on the shelf is white.",
